Id: suid002i
Severity: INFO
Category: filesystem
Check: check_suid
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST AC-6, CM-7; ISO 8.2, 8.18; CE Secure configuration

A setuid file can be written by its group or by any user. Whoever can
write the file can replace it with a program of their own choosing,
which then runs with the file owner's privileges. Remove the write
permission with chmod, or take the setuid bit off if the program does
not need it.

It is INFO because the file named is a directory or not executable,
though others (its group, or anyone) can write it.

Until 3.4.0 this was reported as suid002, without the letter for its level.
